WEBVTT

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:06.120
We should go for ice cream.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.180
Yeah.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:08.820
Mogi-chan.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.250
We're all going to the 
ice cream shop by the station.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.320
Want to come?

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.660
Sorry, not today.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.080
Farewell, sirs.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.210
What are you, a samurai?

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.830
See you tomorrow.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.720
<i>Isao must be waiting for me.</i>

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.410
Have you found it?

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.470
Nope, it's nowhere to be seen.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.370
We found that child oni during setsubun.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.380
I didn't think it'd still be around here.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.280
Let's look over there.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.910
I'm home.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.510
Isao.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.900
Have you been a good boy?

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:06.930
Conny?!

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:09.380
Conny was?

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:10.890
Yeah.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:14.410
It would have been bad if 
someone else found him,

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:16.880
so I thought I'd talk to you about it.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.770
I've been wondering where 
he'd been going every day.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:26.020
I never thought he'd be at your place.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.490
Yeah.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:30.900
I asked Mom, and she said 
he comes almost every day.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.170
It'd be nice if someone could 
take care of him temporarily.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.780
You said it before, too, Kashiwagi.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.110
If we could find a place,

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:46.540
we could leave these kids 
there before we go to school.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:56.900
Hey!

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:57.700
Stop!

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:01.470
Isao...

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.040
<i>Mii-kun can stay at home by himself 
once every two days at least.</i>

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.450
<i>I wonder if he'll learn to stay by himself 
even longer if he's with the others.</i>

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:13.910
All right.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.970
I'll ask someone I know.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.490
I know someone who might be up for it.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.240
An acquaintance?

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:20.960
I'll ask them tomorrow.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.120
Can you give me a day?

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.810
Are you sure that's safe?

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:30.000
We aren't supposed to tell people 
about these guys, are we?

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.250
Yeah.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.270
I can promise those people will be fine.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:10.310
#08
New Places, Strange Places,
Strange Friends

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.950
Thanks for coming so early 
in the morning, Grandpa.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.690
Thanks for taking this on.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.140
It's all right.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:21.440
It gets boring around here for us.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.300
We'll enjoy the company.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.200
Thanks.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.450
His acquaintance was a Buddhist monk statue?

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:35.200
This is the Ojizou statue of Outotsu Shrine.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.930
His nickname is Grandpa.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:38.650
Call me Grandpa or Gramps.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.970
Whatever you'd like.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.970
You're brothers with the eastern 
Outotsu Shrine, aren't you?

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.660
<i>They have siblings?</i>

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.050
Did you know him, too, Tacchan?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.120
Yeah.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.510
I've been coming to this 
shrine for a long time.

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.350
I've known of him.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.970
Sora and Tazuki both wash my back

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:02.270
and leave offerings of dumplings 
and snacks and such.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:05.860
Grandpa, please don't.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.370
<i>They're close.</i>

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:09.740
Nice to meet you.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.830
My name is Motegi Asa.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.980
Nice to meet you. My name is Tachiaki Daichi.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.030
My Mukumuku will be in your care.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.630
Please and thank you.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:22.420
Well, well, thank you for 
the polite introductions.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:29.390
Daichi-kun, behind you...

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.080
Oh, it's Mukumuku.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:35.320
You scared me.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.690
Mukumuku! Your eyes!

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:39.650
Watch the twigs!

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:50.030
Conny, don't smack people's heads.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.790
Do you still have time before school?

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:59.040
Well, I should probably 
say bye and get going.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:03.670
Hey, Sora-chan, I brought lunch for Isao.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:07.550
Oh, you can leave that here with him.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:11.040
S-Sora-chan!

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.680
Sora-kun, behind you!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:14.780
Behind me?

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.570
Sora-chan got taken away!

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:24.620
<i>Holy crap, that's scary.</i>

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:25.310
<i>Holy crap, that's scary.</i>

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:26.060
<i>Holy crap, that's scary.</i>

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.700
<i>S-S-S-Scary...</i>

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:29.930
S-Sora-kun!

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:30.900
Dai-chan!

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.740
Wait, I'm coming!

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:33.620
Hey!

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.130
You there!

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.030
I don't know if you're a monster or what,

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:40.970
but don't you dare do anything to Sora-kun.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.960
Oh, Daichi.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:50.740
This is the god of this place.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.810
I'm sorry for calling you a monster.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.100
I'm sorry we didn't even knock.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:08.430
She offered to let us come inside 
while Mii-kun and the gang stay here.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.400
We'd have to worry about people 
seeing them outside, too.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.120
Thank you.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.240
You guys...

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:20.130
You're free to relax, 
but at least come get your bags.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:26.000
Please and thank you, once again.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:27.500
Thank you.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:32.720
This place is convenient enough 
to come by on our way to school.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:36.800
And if anyone asks, we can just tell 
them we're visiting the shrine.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:40.440
The god's tea is so calming.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.480
I know.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.530
It's so calming that I feel like 
it's made us forget something.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:49.030
School!

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:58.660
I wonder what they're up to about now.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:01.380
Isao's probably napping.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:06.200
I'm sure they'll be better off being with 
each other than being by themselves at home.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:06.940
Yeah.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:07.840
You're right.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.730
Speaking of which, I know this comes late,

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:15.220
but I don't know what to call you two yet.

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:18.750
Can I call you Acchan?

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.370
Hey, it's a new nickname.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:23.030
Um...

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:24.560
Tacchan?

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:25.780
Don't you dare.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:26.860
You give me chills.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.860
Kami-kun, then?

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.810
That's a little better.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.700
It's the anchoring effect.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:38.330
What's that?

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:42.880
For example, if someone asked you to make an 
apple pie, it would seem like a lot of work.

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:47.910
So if they said, "Then can you peel 
an apple instead," it would seem easy,

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:50.420
and you'd be more likely to go with it.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.240
That's the effect.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.220
I see.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:56.050
But peeling an apple is a lot of work, too.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.350
It can turn out lousy-looking.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.850
We're back for you, Mii-kun.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:12.740
I missed you, Isao.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:14.490
Let's go, Conny.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.100
Come on...

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:24.620
I guess they want to play more.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.000
Huh?

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:29.540
Mii-kun, you look more moist than usual.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.700
I mean, you're shining.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.920
<i>He's more plump, I think?</i>

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:38.640
<i>His bandages feel different.</i>

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.440
Did you have fun playing?

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.320
Yeah? Glad to hear.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:56.810
Morning, Grandpa.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:58.780
Morning.

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:07.370
The others are already here today.

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:10.130
Thanks for watching them again, today.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:16.380
Okay, Mii-kun, I'm going to school, now.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:24.140
I'll come back for you after school, okay?

00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:59.380
What was that?

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:07.200
I thought I saw something.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:09.950
I must be imagining things.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.600
"Are you by yourself?"

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:39.270
"Are you lost?"

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.950
"Going up?"

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:50.160
"Let's go together."

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:10.770
It's raining.

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:13.820
The forecast didn't say it was going to rain.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:14.830
I know.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.690
It's really coming down.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:20.780
Shoot, I left the laundry out.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.040
"Do you...

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.550
live here alone?"

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.880
"It's a nice,

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:35.550
spacious home."

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.700
"You should stay here

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.450
until the rain stops!"

00:16:58.530 --> 00:16:59.790
"You're never

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.290
going home."

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.340
"You can have this."

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:21.600
"Eat this mushroom."

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.480
"Maybe he's not lost."

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:17.490
"Maybe he just wanted to get to the shrine."

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:56.240
The rain stopped.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:57.740
Good.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:00.240
I didn't bring an umbrella.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:20.000
Where has Mii-kun gone?

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:23.760
I could help look for him 
if only I could move.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:14.810
Huh? Outside?

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:20.300
And that child oni brought him 
all the way back here, huh?

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:24.990
I'm glad nothing happened.

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:27.690
But don't go out by yourself anymore.

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:28.840
It's dangerous.

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:36.000
Mii-kun, did you get to thank that child oni?

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:40.060
Yeah?

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:41.880
In that case...

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:30.430
Having trouble sleeping?

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:37.130
Don't worry, there are all kinds 
of creatures living there.

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:39.670
I'm sure someone will 
find it and let him know.

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:43.990
I bet he's reading the 
letter right about now.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:44.190
<b>Thank You</b>

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:23.240
Morning, Grandpa.

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:24.920
Good morning.

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:27.690
Sorry about yesterday.

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:29.380
The god hopes to do better today.

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:30.930
She's hard at work.

00:23:38.280 --> 00:23:40.610
She's <i>really</i> hard at work.

00:23:40.610 --> 00:23:41.560
She is.

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:44.570
Thank you, god.

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:47.500
Thanks for watching them again, today!

00:23:50.870 --> 00:23:53.730
I made school uniforms 
for Mii-kun and the others.

00:23:53.730 --> 00:23:55.510
They really liked it.

00:23:55.820 --> 00:23:59.790
I guess they liked having matching clothes.

00:23:59.710 --> 00:24:04.630
Next Episode
Kind Hands, Warm Hands

00:24:00.610 --> 00:24:01.870
<i>How to Keep a Mummy</i>.

00:24:01.870 --> 00:24:03.380
See you next episode.
